    :math-program "(define (max-norm xs)\n  (let ((m (stat/max xs)))\n    (map (lambda (x) (/ x m)) xs)))\n(max-norm '(10 20 30 40))"
    :cs-program "(define (clamp-at-max data cap)\n  ;; Clamp any value that exceeds cap down to cap; uses stat/max to find the current peak.\n  (let ((peak (stat/max data)))\n    (if (<= peak cap) data\n        (map (lambda (x) (if (> x cap) cap x)) data))))\n(clamp-at-max '(5 10 15 20 25) 18)"
    :explanation "stat/max returns the largest; guarded division normalises to [0,1]. Empty case returns 'nan so the operator falls through."
