   (:eng "O(n) scan; returns 'nan on empty." :math "max(x_1, ..., x_n)." :cs "Total on non-empty numeric list."))
  :row-3-dimension ((:setup "The shape is 'upper extreme of an ordered sample'." :rungs ((:domain "statistics (this verb)" :code "(stat/max '(3 1 4 1 5 9))") (:domain "monitoring — max latency or peak load in a window" :code "(define (max-norm xs)\n  (let ((m (stat/max xs)))\n    (map (lambda (x) (/ x m)) xs)))\n(max-norm '(10 20 30 40))") (:domain "order theory — supremum of a finite set" :code "(define (max-norm xs)\n  (let ((m (stat/max xs)))\n    (map (lambda (x) (/ x m)) xs)))\n(max-norm '(10 20 30 40))")) :explanation "Statistics reads it as an order statistic. Monitoring reads it as peak. Order theory reads it as sup. Same operation, three domains." :meta "Shape transfers because supremum is a universal categorical construction on ordered sets.") (:eng "Same call in analytics, monitoring, and math." :math "Sup of a finite ordered set exists and equals the maximum." :cs "The pattern is the base case for supremum on any ordered structure."))
