  :row-3-dimension ((:setup "The shape is 'first-moment center of a distribution' — average." :rungs ((:domain "statistics (this verb)" :code "(stat/mean '(1 2 3 4 5))") (:domain "monitoring — mean latency across a window" :code "(let ((scores '(72 84 68 91 77 85 63 88)))\n  (list ':mean (stat/mean scores) ':median (stat/median scores)\n        ':skew (- (stat/mean scores) (stat/median scores))))") (:domain "probability — expected value of a discrete uniform sample" :code "(let ((scores '(72 84 68 91 77 85 63 88)))\n  (list ':mean (stat/mean scores) ':median (stat/median scores)\n        ':skew (- (stat/mean scores) (stat/median scores))))")) :explanation "Statistics reads it as arithmetic average. Monitoring reads it as expected latency. Probability reads it as sample expectation. Same operation, three domains." :meta "Shape transfers because the first-moment is a universal aggregate.") (:eng "Same call across analytics, ops, and probability." :math "μ = E[X] estimated by (1/n) Σxᵢ." :cs "The pattern generalises to weighted mean."))
