(verb
  :name "stat/mode" :std "Motoi"
  :library "stat"
  :kind "meta"
  :signature "(stat/mode list) -> value | (list value value ...) | 'nan"
  :summary "Find the most-frequent value(s) in a list; multimodal sets → tie list; empty or no-mode → 'nan."
  :explanation "The mode is the value that appears most often in a dataset. `stat/mode` counts occurrences and returns the single most frequent value if there is a unique maximum. If multiple values tie for most frequent (multimodal), it returns them as a list. If the input is empty or no value repeats (all equally rare), it returns the symbol 'nan (not a number). This is useful for finding the \"typical\" categorical value in survey data, game state distributions, or any discrete frequency analysis."
  :examples (
    (:dialect "motoi" :tier "novice" :code "(stat/mode (list 1 2 2 3 2))" :note "Returns 2 (appears 3 times, more than 1 or 3).")
    (:dialect "motoi" :tier "apprentice" :code "(stat/mode '(4 4 4 6 8))" :note "4 appears 3 times; 6 and 8 appear once each. Returns 4.")
    (:dialect "motoi" :tier "intermediate" :code "(stat/mode (list 'red 'blue 'red 'green 'blue))" :note "Returns (red blue) — both colors appear twice; a tie.")
    (:dialect "motoi" :tier "expert" :code "(define (most-common-outcome trials)\n  (let ((results (map (lambda (t) (list-ref t 2)) trials)))\n    (stat/mode results)))\n(most-common-outcome\n  (list\n    (list 0 100 'win)\n    (list 1 105 'win)\n    (list 2 90 'lose)\n    (list 3 95 'win)))" :note "Extract the 3rd element (outcome) from each trial and find the most common; returns 'win.")
    (:dialect "motoi" :tier "master" :code "(define (unimodal? data)\n  ;; Returns #t if stat/mode produces exactly one value (not a list of ties).\n  (let ((m (stat/mode data)))\n    (and (not (eq? m 'nan)) (not (list? m)))))\n(list (unimodal? '(1 2 2 3 2))\n      (unimodal? '(1 1 2 2 3))\n      (unimodal? '(1 2 3 4 5)))" :note "Returns (#t #f #f) — first is unimodal, second bimodal, third all-unique so 'nan.")
  )
  :caveats ("Multimodal data returns a list of tied values, not a single value; caller must check (list? result) vs. (symbol? result)." "Empty list returns 'nan, not an error." "All unique values (each frequency = 1) returns 'nan, not the first value." "'nan is the symbol nan, not a number; use (eq? result 'nan) to test.")
  :drawbacks ("Does not distinguish between data types; (1 '1) counts as two different values." "For large lists, the frequency map can be memory-heavy; consider pre-filtering if data is sparse." "Does not return the frequency; if you need the count, you must use a separate fold or count-frequencies verb.")
  :usecases ("Finding the most common player choice in a game (most-picked class, most-visited location)." "Survey analysis: determining the most popular response to a categorical question." "Data quality: identifying unexpected modal values that might indicate bugs or outliers.")
  :related ("math/avg" "math/sum" "fold-left" "map")
  :learn (:concept "Frequency-based statistics: the mode as a measure of central tendency for categorical data." :prerequisites ("list (core form)" "map (core form)" "fold-left or a manual counting loop") :progression "Combine stat/mode with math/avg and similar verbs to build fuller descriptive statistics; use in decision-making (e.g., if mode = X, do Y).")
  :row-2-audit (
   (:problem "A user-survey lane needs the most-common answer category; the operator has categorical responses and wants the mode with a tie-flag."
    :eng-program "(define responses '(yes no yes yes no maybe yes no))\n(define m (stat/mode responses))\n(list ':mode m ':tie? (list? m))"
    :math-program "(let ((dice-rolls '(1 3 2 4 2 5 2 6 3 3)))\n  (list ':mode (stat/mode dice-rolls) ':freq-3 (length (filter (lambda (x) (= x 3)) dice-rolls))\n        ':freq-2 (length (filter (lambda (x) (= x 2)) dice-rolls))))"
    :cs-program "(define (mode-safe data)\n  ;; Mode with explicit handling of nan and ties.\n  (let ((m (stat/mode data)))\n    (cond ((eq? m 'nan) (list ':result 'no-mode))\n          ((list? m)  (list ':result 'tied ':values m))\n          (else       (list ':result 'unique ':value m)))))\n(list (mode-safe '(1 2 2 3 2)) (mode-safe '(1 1 2 2)) (mode-safe '(1 2 3)))"
    :explanation "stat/mode returns a value or a list of tied values; the operator uses list? to detect ties for the audit."
    :meta "stat/mean and stat/median don't apply to categorical data. stat/mode is the only central-tendency verb that respects category-typed data.")
   (:eng "Empty returns 'nan; ties surface as list; O(n) with a frequency map." :math "Mode = argmax_v |{i : x_i = v}|." :cs "O(n) time, O(k) space for the freq map."))
  :row-3-dimension ((:setup "The shape is 'most frequent element in a labelled collection'." :rungs ((:domain "statistics (this verb)" :code "(stat/mode '(a b b c b))") (:domain "log analysis — most-common error code in a stream" :code "(let ((dice-rolls '(1 3 2 4 2 5 2 6 3 3)))\n  (list ':mode (stat/mode dice-rolls) ':freq-3 (length (filter (lambda (x) (= x 3)) dice-rolls))\n        ':freq-2 (length (filter (lambda (x) (= x 2)) dice-rolls))))") (:domain "probability — argmax of a discrete probability mass function" :code "(let ((dice-rolls '(1 3 2 4 2 5 2 6 3 3)))\n  (list ':mode (stat/mode dice-rolls) ':freq-3 (length (filter (lambda (x) (= x 3)) dice-rolls))\n        ':freq-2 (length (filter (lambda (x) (= x 2)) dice-rolls))))")) :explanation "Statistics reads it as mode. Logs read it as top-error. Probability reads it as argmax of pmf. Same operation, three domains." :meta "Shape transfers because argmax-frequency is universal on categorical/discrete data.") (:eng "Same call in analytics, log dashboards, and probability." :math "Mode is the peak of the empirical distribution." :cs "The pattern generalises to top-k via a bounded heap."))
  :row-4-proof (
   (:claim "The frequency of the mode is ≥ frequency of any other value."
    :eng-program "(define d '(1 2 2 3 3 3 4))\n(define m (stat/mode d))\n(define (count v xs) (length (filter (lambda (x) (equal? x v)) xs)))\n(list (>= (count m d) (count 1 d)) (>= (count m d) (count 2 d)))"
    :math-program "(define (mode-frequency-max? data)\n  (let ((m (stat/mode data))\n        (cnt (lambda (v) (length (filter (lambda (x) (equal? x v)) data)))))\n    (if (list? m) #t  ;; ties all equal\n        (let ((mf (cnt m)))\n          (not (find (lambda (v) (> (cnt v) mf)) data))))))\n(mode-frequency-max? '(4 4 4 6 8))"
    :cs-program "(define (frequencies xs)\n  (let loop ((rest xs) (acc '()))\n    (if (null? rest) acc\n        (let* ((v (car rest))\n               (cell (assoc v acc)))\n          (loop (cdr rest)\n                (if cell\n                    (map (lambda (p) (if (equal? (car p) v) (cons v (+ (cdr p) 1)) p)) acc)\n                    (cons (cons v 1) acc)))))))\n(define (max-freq-value xs)\n  (let* ((freq (frequencies xs))\n         (peak (apply max (map cdr freq))))\n    (map car (filter (lambda (p) (= (cdr p) peak)) freq))))\n(max-freq-value '(1 2 2 3 3 3 4))"
    :invariant "∀ data. count(stat/mode(data), data) ≥ count(v, data) ∀v∈data"
